example.apply(exampleObj, ["Sarthak"]);
// "Sarthak runs sarthakworks";`},{type:"paragraph",text:"The difference between call and apply is that apply accepts arguments in an array, while call accepts it normally."},{type:"paragraph",text:"When using bind, we can create a new function with the new values and store it in a variable, and then use it further. It creates fresh permanent binding without affecting the original function."},{type:"code",language:"javascript",value:`const exampleObj = {
